# DATA_DIR is resolved relative to the working directory, so a SQLite file can land
# either under apps/api/ or at the repo root depending on how the API was started.
**/data/*.db
**/data/*.db-shm
**/data/*.db-wal
apps/api/data/*.db-journal
apps/api/data/uploads/*
!apps/api/data/uploads/.gitkeep
.DS_Store
*.log
.vite/

# Vercel CLI project link and local build output
.vercel/

.vercel
.env*

# Generated by "build:fn" (esbuild bundle of vercel-entry.ts). Checked in deliberately:
# Vercel's git-triggered build validates vercel.json's "functions": {"api/index.js": ...}
# glob against the freshly cloned source tree BEFORE running buildCommand, so if this file
# doesn't already exist in the repo, the build fails immediately with "unmatched-function-
# pattern" and buildCommand never even runs. A `vercel deploy` from local files never hit
# this because it uploads whatever's already on disk. buildCommand still regenerates this
# file from scratch on every deploy — the committed copy only exists to satisfy that
# pre-build check; treat it as disposable and don't hand-edit it.

# graphify knowledge graph — generated by `graphify update .`, ~2.5MB, and the
# sidecars record absolute paths from whichever machine built it. Regenerate rather
# than check in.
graphify-out/

# Per-machine Claude Code preferences (settings.json, the shared one, is checked in).
.claude/settings.local.json
